<h1>Yolonda Morris</h1>
<p>Illinois House, 9th District, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026. Party: Democratic. Incumbent.</p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>No campaign site found. Her ilga.gov biography says she has advocated for the Fight for 15 minimum wage campaign, safe staffing, and child care for all; her office site lists committee work on public safety appropriations, health care access, housing, human services, mental health and addiction, and public health.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Certified nursing assistant for 26 years and a former SEIU union organizer; appointed to the House in September 2023.</p>
